      "text": "Let's denote the two numbers as \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) where \\( x > y \\). We are given two pieces of information:\n\n1. The sum of the two numbers is 6:\n\\[ x + y = 6 \\]\n\n2. The difference of their squares is 12:\n\\[ x^2 - y^2 = 12 \\]\n\nWe recognize that the difference of squares can be factored as:\n\\[ x^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y) \\]\n\nUsing the first piece of information, we substitute \\( x + y \\) with 6:\n\\[ x^2 - y^2 = 6(x - y) \\]\n\\[ 12 = 6(x - y) \\]\n\\[ x - y = \\frac{12}{6} \\]\n\\[ x - y = 2 \\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( x + y = 6 \\)\n2. \\( x - y = 2 \\)\n\nWe can solve this system by adding the two equations together:\n\\[ (x + y) + (x - y) = 6 + 2 \\]\n\\[ 2x = 8 \\]\n\\[ x = 4 \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( x = 4 \\) back into the first equation:\n\\[ 4 + y = 6 \\]\n\\[ y = 2 \\]\n\nThus, the two numbers are \\( x = 4 \\) and \\( y = 2 \\). The positive difference between these two numbers is:\n\\[ x - y = 4 - 2 = 2 \\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference of the two numbers is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
