      "text": "Let's denote the two numbers by \\( x \\) and \\( y \\), with \\( x > y \\).\n\nWe are given two pieces of information:\n1. The sum of the two numbers is 6:\n   \\[\n   x + y = 6\n   \\]\n2. The difference of their squares is 12:\n   \\[\n   x^2 - y^2 = 12\n   \\]\n\nWe recognize that the difference of squares can be factored as:\n\\[\nx^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y)\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given value of \\( x + y \\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n(x + y)(x - y) = 12\n\\]\n\\[\n6(x - y) = 12\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x - y \\), we divide both sides by 6:\n\\[\nx - y = \\frac{12}{6} = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the positive difference of the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
